  (text_box "PS1 (HLK-PM12) is an encapsulated power supply, which converts the AC input voltage into 12V DC.\nThe power supply maximum power is 3W. \n\nC1 is a X2 safety capacitor. C2 is the power supply output filtering capacitor."
    (at 106.045 97.155 0) (size 53.34 13.97)
    (stroke (width 0.3) (type default))
    (fill (type color) (color 194 194 194 1))
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 27ed087e-d053-4b35-aaae-8c61b4760313)
  )
  (text_box "R8 is a LDR, which is exposed to the external environment.\n\nThe MCU's input receives the resulting voltage from that voltage divider."
    (at 149.86 212.725 0) (size 38.1 13.97)
    (stroke (width 0.3) (type default))
    (fill (type color) (color 194 194 194 1))
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 2b685472-7aa1-4d75-8dd7-1468ea36d65a)
  )
  (text_box "One of the MCU's digital outputs is used to control the K1 relay through Q1 transistor (2N7002H).\n\nU3 optocoupler (PC817) isolates the output from the power circuit.\n\nWhen the output's logic level is LOW, the transistor is not conducting and the relay coil is de-energized.\nWhen the output's logic level is HIGH, the transistor is conducting and the relay coil is energized.\n\nThe R5 resistor limits the optocoupler input current. The R6 resistor pull the transistor gate down.\nThe D1 diode act as a flyback diode. J5 connector goes to the load."
    (at 52.07 208.915 0) (size 85.09 28.575)
    (stroke (width 0.3) (type default))
    (fill (type color) (color 194 194 194 1))
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 2e01c951-3fe7-415e-8c71-73ba48e130f7)
  )
  (text_box "J2 connector provides access to the MCU module's serial bus.\n\nJ3 connector needs a jumper to connect the MCU's FLASH pin to 3V3 or GND.\nGPIO0 connected to GND is used to program the microcontroller.\nGPIO0 connected to 3V3 is used to run the code."
    (at 320.675 98.425 0) (size 48.895 20.32)
    (stroke (width 0.3) (type default))
    (fill (type color) (color 194 194 194 1))
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 46fd416b-0715-44df-a112-2672222ea45a)
  )
  (text_box "D2 LED indicates when the 12V bus is powered.\n\nR7 resistor limits the current through the LED."
    (at 149.86 173.355 0) (size 38.1 12.7)
    (stroke (width 0.3) (type default))
    (fill (type color) (color 194 194 194 1))
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 5f12893b-28c1-4c16-8597-bc4db7af360b)
  )
  (text_box "U2 (ESP-12E MODULE) is a microcontroller with WiFi capabilities. It is responsible for all the logic and controll functions of the module.\n\nSome of its pins must be pulled up or down. This is done through the R1, R2 and R3 resistors.\n\nC5 capacitor is a filtering capacitor for the power input."
    (at 229.235 121.285 0) (size 78.74 17.78)
    (stroke (width 0.3) (type default))
    (fill (type color) (color 194 194 194 1))
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 61ca9d03-5dfd-4838-944d-cbc7a9fda28b)
  )
  (text_box "U1 voltage regulator (AMS1117-3.3) steps the 12V voltage down to 3,3V, with maximum output current of 1A.\n \nC3 and C4 capacitors are filtering capacitors, suggested on the regulator's datasheet."
    (at 172.085 97.155 0) (size 43.18 16.51)
    (stroke (width 0.3) (type default))
    (fill (type color) (color 194 194 194 1))
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 73c80b95-d410-460a-9594-789f24033bce)
  )
  (text_box "J1 is the terminal block intended for:\n- Terminal 1 - LINE\n- Terminal 2 - NEUTRAL\n- Terminal 3 - PE\n- Terminal 4 - Switch return\n- Terminal 5 - Load"
    (at 52.705 94.615 0) (size 40.64 13.97)
    (stroke (width 0.3) (type default))
    (fill (type color) (color 194 194 194 1))
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 9fd5fdee-c14a-422c-aa20-b633532581c0)
  )
  (text_box "The voltage coming from the switch input is dropped on a capacitive dropper composed by C6, R10 and R11. The impedance is approximately 110 kohms at 60Hz.\n\nL1 is a ferrite bead, intended to reduce high frequency coupling on the switch input.\n\nR9 is the bleeder resistor, which discharge the voltage stored on C6.\n\nU4 (H11AA1) connects the MCU's input to GND when there is a voltage input present.\n\nR12 and C7 compose a RC low-pass filter which cut-off frequency of 160 Hz, approximately. "
    (at 200.66 194.945 0) (size 77.47 33.02)
    (stroke (width 0.3) (type default))
    (fill (type color) (color 194 194 194 1))
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid c56b802c-40e8-40fe-82a6-45152af67e67)
  )

